  <title>Caret navigation</title>
  <p>
    Caret navigation lets you move through text by character, word, and line, as well as to the
    beginning and end of lines and documents.
  </p>
  <p>
    Caret navigation is not limited to web content. It is intended to work in text objects,
    including terminals, when the application exposes the needed text information to assistive
    technologies.
  </p>
  <p>
    When browse mode is active, you can use caret navigation commands to read and move through
    document content. If focus mode is active, switch to browse mode before using caret
    navigation commands. In text objects where browse mode is not supported, you can manually
    turn Orca's caret navigation on or off with <keyseq>
      <key>Orca Modifier</key>
      <key>F12</key>
    </keyseq>. This command
    changes the current session across applications; it does not save a preference.
  </p>
  <p>
    Orca can also manage text selection when you hold <key>Shift</key> while using these navigation
    commands. Text selection is disabled by default because not all applications provide the
    support Orca needs to manage selections. Avoid enabling it globally. Instead, enable it in
    application-specific preferences only for applications where Orca's selection support is
    needed and you have verified that it works correctly.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-caret-navigation">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Documents</gui> category, <gui>Caret navigation</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Caret navigation</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca provides text navigation using the arrow keys, Home, and End. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Automatic focus mode</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca switches to focus mode when caret navigation lands on an interactive widget.
          Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Text selection</gui>: Controls whether
          Shift with caret navigation extends text selections. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Layout mode</gui>: Controls whether Orca
          presents each full visual line or treats each object as if it were on a separate line.
          Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
